            <ArticleTitle>[Comparative evaluation of the results of conservative and surgical treatment of unstable angina at long-term follow-up].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two hundred patients with unstable angina were examined. Of those, 100 were on medication only, while another 100 had undergone aortocoronary shunting. Five-year survival rate was higher, and the quality of life was better, in the surgical patients, as compared to conservative cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
